{1000}{37c








Social Utopian Societies:  Vormantown
by
Merton K. Vorman










}
{1001}{37l
	The varied and specific reasons behind my social experiments here in Vormantown were birthed many years ago during my research at both Tarant University, and later on during my extended stay at the Tullan Library.  It is my opinion that society at large suffers not from a lack of civility, nor from a lack of understanding about the social code.  No, what I believe, and what I have endeavored to prove here in Vormantown, is that man (as well as gnomes, dwarves and all other sentient and otherwise rational races, not including orcs, ogres and the lesser barbarian hordes) has never had the proper framework to express his true rationality and intellect.  Here, in Vormantown, I am attempting to provide that framework, and to show the social and cultural heights that a well-balanced community can aspire to.

	To truly understand the relationship between behavior and environment, one must have a strong grasp of the psycho-sociological theories that have preceded the present day model.  One might be so inclined to read the elven masters, Ger’in and Bree’Nar, as well as the gnomish existentialists from before the Age of Legends.  This is merely a foundation from which to grow on; one cannot ignore the works of the dwarf Odin StoneHands, and the collected manuscripts of the Triock Collective.  Taking these works into account, one can begin to build upon more than a millennium of...}



{1010}{37c









Geographical Oddities of the Ivory Lake, Vol. 1
by
Terence Gilmore, Phd, MD.
Tarant University, 1902










}
{1011}{37l
	The body of water known as the Ivory Lake has a number of strange characteristics that make it geographically unique in Arcanum.  Being situated between Sorrel’s Rock and the Erriwind Forest, there are marked differences in both flora and fauna, as well as unpredictable weather and uncommon geographical phenomenon.  But, most importantly, it is the presence of the Stone Heart Clan Dwarves and the Ter’elon Elves that give this remote lake its most fascinating characteristics.
}
{1012}{37l
	Because of these two groups, one of which is inherently magickal, and the other which utilizes technology, the entire area is a conflict of physical law.  These ancient forces, pushing and pulling against one another, increase the chances for inexplicable phenomenon;  written histories of the lands surrounding Ivory Lake have described all manner of strange events.  In 1536, there is a well-documented sighting of three trees which seemed to be “dancing” with one another, fully uprooted and floating above the ground.  There was the unexplained rock storms of 1754, as well as the mile-wide whirlpool which broke the lake’s surface for 5 weeks in 1865.
}
{1013}{37l
	Countless legends have sprung up because of these “mystical” oddities, and the area has become a favorite pilgrimage of those interested in the arcane and the paranormal.  More than a few clairvoyants have targeted the area as some sort of “gateway” for spirits and such, as well as being a place where their powers are amplified and focused….
}


{1020}{37c








Arcanomicon:
Selected Excerpts
Translated by W'yne Bor'en











}
{1021}{37l
	...And lo, there were two forces, and each was of another world, and they fought against one another and peace would not be made between them.

	But a man would come, in the place of power and ivory, who would bring the two forces together and make them his own.

	And that man, with the forces held in each hand, would be as a god and pass judgment on all from above.

	But woe to he who plays at god but is not.  For peace will not be made by he who knows not the path, and war will be brought upon him and his progeny, and he will be lost in deaths shadow, and his line will come to an end...}
